## Source audit

**7 inline / 0 vague / 0 untagged** (was 0 / 5 / 1). Getting there required a script fix: `blog-source-audit.mjs` didn't know Le Figaro, Le Monde, Financial Times, Big Technology Podcast or École Polytechnique, and its `TIME` entry was listed as `Time` — matching is case-sensitive, so every TIME-sourced quote in this vertical graded vague. I re-ran four other drafts to confirm no regression. Worth knowing for future passes: the attribution window is 120 characters before the quote, so an outlet named earlier in a long sentence silently doesn't count.

`blog-lint`: 0 fail, 0 warn. 3,897 words, inside the 3,200–3,900 band, and contrast pairs went from 0 strong / 1 comparative to 0 / 0. Getting back under the ceiling took real cutting — I added roughly 650 words and had to find about the same again, mostly from duplicated anecdotes (Chinchilla was explained twice, "never showed off" appeared twice, the deflation inventory stacked five items) and two summarizing paragraphs around the table.

## Worth an editor's eye

Type confidence stays medium-high, and now for a sharper reason: February 2024 is genuine disconfirming pressure on the sovereignty-as-conviction reading, and the July weights release is the rebuttal. Whether I've struck that balance fairly rather than protectively is a human call. The Microsoft stake is also reported as ~€15M by Euronews/FT and ~$16M elsewhere; the draft hedges with "reported at around."
